    "created_at": "2022-04-22T15:14:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-22T15:14:30Z",
    "body": "> However, that assumes a microtask can be enqueued without a corresponding task, right? I don't think that's something we mean to support.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure. Basically saying that we don't support this means we don't support implementations enqueuing microtasks, unless they do so from inside a task.\r\n\r\nI think there are at least some instances of this, e.g. all the calls to \"await a stable state\".",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
